**How to implement.** S6 prerequisite/closure for 001 §H and §S6: the shared item contracts MUST land here so experiment copying includes item mapping before S7. The copy panel's item mapping as semantic messages of the kit window (the S7.2 brief: after the experiments are picked, a mapping table lists every item they use, each with 'map to existing item' or 'add'; the S6 mapper's request: the kit bar's copy panel gains its choice; .spec-md §4 'UI'). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2: (1) `KitCopySource` (step 225) gains `items : Item list` (the source kit's items, read when it opens) and `itemRows : ItemCopyRow list` (the mapping table, step 221), each documented in one line. (2) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `ChooseCopiedItem of ItemId * ItemCopyChoice`, documented in one line: a press of a choice of the mapping table. (3) Arms. `OpenCopySource` (step 225) also reads the source's `readItems ()` after its experiments, an `Error e` closing what was opened with step 225's text; the source opens with its items and no row. `ToggleCopiedExperiment` (step 225) MUST first resolve Experiment.itemsUsedBy for the chosen experiments against src.items; on Ok used it sets itemRows to ItemCopyRow.copyRowsFor used model.kitItems src.itemRows, and on Error it keeps the previous selection and rows, reports the typed diagnostic and writes nothing, so a row appears at its default with the first chosen experiment that uses its item, keeps the user's choice while used, and goes when no chosen experiment uses it. `ChooseCopiedItem (id, choice)` sets the choice of the row whose `sourceItem.id` is `id`, and changes nothing without such a row or a source; it writes nothing. `CopyChosenExperiments` passes `src.itemRows` where step 227 passed `[]`; its status after an `Ok` that added items is `Copied <n> experiment(s) and added <m> item(s) from <the source kit's name>.`, and with no item added step 225's text; an `Error e` keeps the panel with step 225's text. No preview, undo or other message is added. Every record expression that builds a `KitCopySource` in the tests gains the two fields (`KitWindowModelTests`' read-only copy fact and `KitWindowTests`' open-source fact, steps 225, 226), their assertions unchanged. Tests, in `KitWindowModelTests`, over step 225's folder kits: the source, made as step 225's and closed before a fact opens it, holds E1, whose setup binds the `PresetIds.source600` preset by its entry id, and E2, whose setup binds `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1, recorded through `recordExperiment` (step 149), and the items `Laser600` (`SourcePresetChoice` of that preset) and `QZ` (`StackSampleChoice` of that sample at version 1), recorded through `recordItem` (step 219); the target holds a `Laser600` item of the same preset under another id. `choosing experiments lists the items they use, each at its default`: after `OpenCopySource`, `itemRows` is empty; toggling E2 lists QZ with `AddCopiedItem`; toggling E1 too lists Laser600 with `MapOntoKitItem` of the target's Laser600, then QZ; toggling E2 off leaves Laser600 alone. `the user's choice for an item is kept and copied`: with E1 and E2 chosen, `ChooseCopiedItem` of Laser600 with `AddCopiedItem`, then `CopyChosenExperiments`, leave the target folder holding `Laser600 (2).item-json` and `QZ.item-json`, `kitItems` the target's Laser600, `Laser600 (2)` and QZ, and `kitStatus` `Copied 2 experiment(s) and added 2 item(s) from <the source's name>.`. `a choice the copy refuses keeps the panel and writes nothing`: with QZ written into the target under its own id first, choosing E2 maps QZ onto it by default; `ChooseCopiedItem` of QZ with `AddCopiedItem` and `CopyChosenExperiments` keep the panel, set `kitStatus` starting `The experiments could not be copied`, and write nothing. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. Every source experiment in these fixtures MUST name the actual source ItemIds in its descriptors. Extend `the user's choice for an item is kept and copied` with a MapOntoKitItem branch choosing a differently identified target of the same preset: close and reopen the target, resolve the copied experiment and assert that exact target id and parameters; assert the unchosen same-preset piece is excluded. `choosing an experiment with a dangling physical binding reports its id and writes nothing` MUST inject only the missing ItemId into a valid loaded source, assert the typed diagnostic and unchanged selection, rows and target files.

**Acceptance.** After a mapping choice is dispatched and Copy completes, the reopened experiment MUST resolve the chosen physical target or the added source identity, independently of shared presets; a dangling source binding MUST report its id without changing selection or files; constructor-unit-tests, selected ui-tests, ui-smoke, build, elevation and the s22 invariants MUST pass.
